[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. Its own table already disagrees: it finds two
causes, and its footnote sets a third kind of report aside. Read by what the reports say, not by
their subject line, #4471 holds three problems. Each one now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix will not close #4471. Form bookings from booking-v3 tenants and the one-day
moves need their own fixes.
</Callout>

## The split

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

Counted the desk's way, from `reports-4471.json` as exported: one report per id (the export repeats
some), cause by tenant from `src/lib/kb/causes.ts`, one-day moves from `desk-notes.json`. A one-day
report stays counted under the cause it is filed under, as in the desk's own table below.
Rules in `src/lib/kb/problems.ts`.

## The three problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first.** Every tenant on file writes the day
first, so 7 April comes out as 4 July. App, email and form bookings on booking-v2 all go through
it. This is the bug the queued fix is for.

**`hint`: booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field.** People type what the hint tells
them, month first, and the form reads the date the tenant's way, day first. Only form bookings at
booking-v3 tenants. Fixing the parser does not fix this: the hint is wrong, not the reading.

**`one-day`: the date moves by one day.** No day and month swap here: Tuesday 12 May becomes
Monday 11 May, a meeting lands on Tuesday in Lisbon and Monday in Toronto. That points at time zones
or the day boundary, not at the parser. The desk saw this (`desk-notes.json`) and files these under
`parser` by tenant, so they count there too; the time-zone fix is separate.

<OneDayReports />

## Why one ticket hid three

- Duplicates were merged on subject alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
  "Date is wrong" fits all three problems.
- Intake tags guess from the reporter's browser, not the tenant, so they do not name the cause.
  The table below shows how far they are off.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Since 5 October

Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October. That closes two of the three problems, not all of them:

- `parser`: **fixed** (`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`). [#1](https://github.com/claritycodeweb/mega-what-it-shows/issues/1) closed.
- `hint`: **won't fix**, the booking-v3 form is retired. [#2](https://github.com/claritycodeweb/mega-what-it-shows/issues/2) closed as not planned.
- `one-day`: **still open.** Neither change touches time zones or the day boundary.
  [#3](https://github.com/claritycodeweb/mega-what-it-shows/issues/3) stays open.

<Callout kind="warn">
Closing #4471 does not close the one-day moves. Do not merge a new one-day report into #4471 or #1;
it belongs on #3.
</Callout>

## For the desk

- Before merging a date report into an open ticket, check tenant, form and channel (the
  [explorer](/kb/triage/dedupe) does this), and read the body for a one-day move.
- Keep #4471 for history; track what is left on #3.

